---
import Frame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';

const items = [
  {
    title: 'How local previews work',
    body: 'Use prepared sample data, inspect each state and reset whenever you want to begin again.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Privacy and data boundaries',
    body: 'No connected accounts, uploads or remote search. Learn exactly what stays in your browser.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Get real website help',
    body: 'Website enquiries belong with the real creator, ISMAIL. PROWORKS has no fictional support service.',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Guides" items={items}>
  <section class="container section reading" id="guide-context">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CONTEXT GOES A LONG WAY</p>
      <h2>Questions worth answering clearly.</h2>
      <p>
        These guides explain the concept and its working examples. They are not
        a customer helpdesk, service agreement or promise of support
        availability.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each answer opens with a native disclosure, including when JavaScript is
        unavailable. Link directly to an answer to share its context.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/compare/">
        Choose a demo →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">KEYBOARD QUICK START</p>
      <h2>Move through the interface at your pace.</h2>
      <p>
        Tab moves to the next interactive control; Shift+Tab moves back. Use
        Enter to follow links, Space or Enter for buttons, and arrow keys to
        change a radio selection or select option.
      </p>
      <p>
        Escape closes the product disclosure first, then the mobile navigation.
        Focus returns to the relevant trigger.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Reset and recover</h3>
      <p>
        Use Reset demo in Workflows to restore all stages. Clear search and
        filters in Knowledge to show every sample document. Reset dashboard in
        Insights returns to the weekly fixture. Reloading also resets the local
        state.
      </p>
      <h3>When JavaScript is unavailable</h3>
      <p>
        You can still read the stage descriptions, open sample document
        excerpts, inspect the initial reporting table and browse the site.
        Controls that need scripting are hidden with an explanation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Frame>
